('deb4987d-c19e-5270-8e70-9682668d72ee'::uuid, 'Physiology (Paper 2)', 'GIT and Liver', 'The hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal (HPA) axis:', '["Regulates only appetite mediated physiological mechanism","Controls digestion directly mediated physiological mechanism","Controls only water balance mediated physiological mechanism","Mediates stress response and affects gut permeability and immune function","Has no relation to gut mediated physiological mechanism"]'::jsonb, 'Mediates stress response and affects gut permeability and immune function', 'Stress activates HPA axis -> cortisol -> alters gut barrier and motility.'),
('c0b48dce-05a5-5578-80d7-c9ddc13401e0'::uuid, 'Physiology (Paper 2)', 'GIT and Liver', 'Visceral hypersensitivity in IBS involves:', '["Complete loss of sensation","Decreased gut sensation","Decreased secretion only","Enhanced perception of normal gut stimuli","Increased peristalsis only"]'::jsonb, 'Enhanced perception of normal gut stimuli', 'Central and peripheral sensitization contribute to pain in IBS.'),
('5773d8d5-a651-5ed9-8fb5-a37686908fbe'::uuid, 'Physiology (Paper 2)', 'GIT and Liver', 'The gut is sometimes called the:', '["Fifth organ","Second brain","Accessory liver","Primary brain","Third kidney"]'::jsonb, 'Second brain', 'The ENS contains ~500 million neurons and uses over 30 neurotransmitters.'),
('c789b8de-e682-5ab9-ad5c-4adb0a894a63'::uuid, 'Physiology (Paper 2)', 'GIT and Liver', 'Serotonin (5-HT) in the gut regulates:', '["Only pain mediated physiological mechanism","Only absorption mediated physiological mechanism","Only motility mediated physiological mechanism","Motility, secretion, and vagal signaling","Only secretion mediated physiological mechanism"]'::jsonb, 'Motility, secretion, and vagal signaling', 'Enterochromaffin cells release 5-HT which acts on ENS and vagal afferents.'),
('feb71e11-97cc-5daa-b288-57844c760c88'::uuid, 'Physiology (Paper 2)', 'GIT and Liver', 'Antidepressants (SSRIs) can affect gut function by:', '["Inhibiting acid secretion mediated physiological mechanism","Altering 5-HT availability in the ENS, affecting motility and sensation","Blocking dopamine mediated physiological mechanism","Stimulating bile flow mediated physiological mechanism","Directly killing bacteria mediated physiological mechanism"]'::jsonb, 'Altering 5-HT availability in the ENS, affecting motility and sensation', 'SSRIs may worsen or improve IBS symptoms depending on baseline motility.'),
('57b1bd9e-c246-5da1-8a10-e731c8b6e950'::uuid, 'Physiology (Paper 2)', 'GIT and Liver', 'Gut microbiota composition is influenced by:', '["Diet, antibiotics, stress, and mode of delivery","Only genetics mediated physiological mechanism","Only diet mediated physiological mechanism","Only antibiotics mediated physiological mechanism","Only age mediated physiological mechanism"]'::jsonb, 'Diet, antibiotics, stress, and mode of delivery', 'C-section vs vaginal delivery dramatically affects early microbiome.'),
('e46f198b-bdca-5225-b279-8dab151e3787'::uuid, 'Physiology (Paper 2)', 'GIT and Liver', 'Dysbiosis (microbiota imbalance) is linked to:', '["No diseases mediated physiological mechanism","Only neurological diseases mediated physiological mechanism","Only metabolic diseases mediated physiological mechanism","Only gut diseases mediated physiological mechanism","IBS, IBD, obesity, depression, and Parkinson disease"]'::jsonb, 'IBS, IBD, obesity, depression, and Parkinson disease', 'Gut-brain axis involvement is increasingly recognized in diverse disorders.'),
('27f1af16-c6e1-561f-a649-38dab5a30fbb'::uuid, 'Physiology (Paper 2)', 'GIT and Liver', 'The enteric glial cells function:', '["Only immune function","Only nutrient supply","Like astrocytes in CNS","Only structural support","Only waste removal"]'::jsonb, 'Like astrocytes in CNS', 'Enteric glia also regulate intestinal barrier integrity.'),
('d68d097c-104f-5c6b-98b8-3018c326ea17'::uuid, 'Physiology (Paper 2)', 'GIT and Liver', 'The blood-brain barrier and gut barrier share which characteristic?', '["Both are composed of endothelial cells only","Both are regulated by tight junctions and affected by inflammation","Both are impermeable to all substances","Both are regulated by microglia only","Both are absent in neonates"]'::jsonb, 'Both are regulated by tight junctions and affected by inflammation', 'Increased intestinal permeability (leaky gut) may contribute to systemic inflammation and CNS effects.'),
('fbc63c3a-5b28-5995-a262-12add49867f7'::uuid, 'Physiology (Paper 2)', 'GIT and Liver', 'Fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT) is effective for:', '["Recurrent Clostridium difficile infection","Obesity mediated physiological mechanism","IBS mediated physiological mechanism","IBD mediated physiological mechanism","All GI diseases mediated physiological mechanism"]'::jsonb, 'Recurrent Clostridium difficile infection', 'FMT restores normal microbiota; >90% effective for recurrent C diff.');
